-- Brief every computerUse subagent that submits a payment: a bank check after it submits is a human step, so it doesn't submit the payment again, keeps the tab open, and reports starting with "Bank verification:", with what the check asks and the amount. When its brief says the user was asked to approve it, the bank check is a step the user already approved: it fills a code only by the value name the brief gives and presses the bank's submit only once that fill's result is back, since calls made together run at once, or just presses submit when the brief says the code is already filled;
+- Brief every computerUse subagent that submits a payment: a bank check after it submits is a human step, so it doesn't submit the payment again, keeps the tab open, and reports `Status: blocked` with `Blocker: bank_verification`, with what the check asks and the amount. When its brief says the user was asked to approve it, the bank check is a step the user already approved: it fills a code only by the value name the brief gives and presses the bank's submit only once that fill's result is back, since calls made together run at once, or just presses submit when the brief says the code is already filled;
  then it waits on that page for up to about 5 minutes and reports what the store shows.
